    size_t len = strlen(str);
    while (isspace(str[len-1])) {
        str[len-1] = '\0';
        len--;
    }
}
```
This function uses the `isspace` function to check if the last character of the string is a whitespace character, and if so, it removes it from the string by setting its value to `\0`. It continues to do this until there are no more trailing whitespace characters. The `size_t` type is used to store the length of the string, which is necessary for the `isspace` function.

The code also uses the `printf` function to print the argument provided by the user twice, with and without trimming the trailing whitespace. The `return 0` statement at the end of the program ensures that it exits successfully.']

